    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d162">

                <pb facs="0167" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.61/916: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-02T15:00:00+03:00">January 2, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 2—12:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. The British Ambassador<anchor n="95" xml:id="d162-f1"/> told me this morning
                    that he has continued to maintain his attitude of aloofness towards the Soviet
                    Government and that he has not seen any of the higher officials of the
                    Commissariat for Foreign Affairs since November 19.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d162-f1" n="95" xml:id="d162-f1-content">
